I closed #1119 with one comment. I left the other 11 issues alone because this session made no progress on any of them.

• #1119 — fixed and closed. Commit f1eb6731 adds the test that checks every provider's default model: every_provider_default_has_a_preset_or_a_stated_reason. I ran it again here and it passes. The comment explains each default that changes what a user with no config gets:
  • xai: grok-4 → grok-4.7. It's cheaper.
  • mistral: mistral-large-latest → mistral-large-4. It costs more and is still a preview. I moved it because the old guessed limit cut long outputs (like file writes) short at 4096 tokens, and Mistral lists mistral-large-4 as Large 3's replacement.
  • zai: glm-4-plus → glm-5.3. Output costs about 6x more. I moved it because the old id isn't on Z.ai's pricing page, so it may not be served anymore.
  
  The comment also says these users move without being told, and that the old ids still work with --model. The other providers keep their defaults, each with a written reason. For six of them that reason is why they still have no preset.
• The comment needed one fix. The shell swallowed the $2 in the xai price, so it read "(/$6". I edited that comment in place to "$2/$6" instead of posting a second one.
